  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "A desert scribal culture that binds survival, learning, and justice into sacred measure.",
    "one_paragraph": "Sulqaim cities rise where caravans meet wells and canals, each ward governed by registrars who track grain, debt, and water with almost liturgical precision. Their priests teach that law is mercy in a harsh land, because only measured obligations keep famine and vendetta from devouring the weak. Foreigners are welcomed to the market and the library, but anyone who tampers with weights, records, or public cisterns is treated as an enemy of the whole people."
